# OPP3a — immutable caching for content-hashed build assets
# (openproduct-performance).
#
# Next fingerprints every file under `/_next/static/` — the hash is in the
# filename — so a content change always produces a NEW URL and a stale cached
# copy becomes unreachable rather than wrong. They are therefore safe to cache
# for a year with no revalidation.
#
# WHAT WAS HAPPENING INSTEAD. The 2026-09-08 production probe read this from
# `openproduct.live`:
#
#     GET /_next/static/chunks/webpack-ebd92b9e6361651a.js
#     cf-cache-status: HIT
#     cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
#
# The `HIT` is the zone cache working. The `max-age=0, must-revalidate` beside
# it is the Workers Assets default, which nobody had looked at: it makes the
# browser send a conditional request for every chunk on every repeat visit and
# on every navigation. A 304 is cheap, and one per chunk per page is not —
# and OPP1 turned every navigation into a client-side one, which is exactly
# when a browser goes back for its chunks.
#
# THE PLATFORM ALREADY DID THIS. `apps/web-console-next/public/_headers` is
# PERF10, shipped and verified live in #305. openproduct became its own product
# before that landed and never inherited it; this is the same file with this
# product's own measurement behind it.
#
# Files in this `public/` directory are copied to the asset root
# (`.open-next/assets/`) by the @opennextjs/cloudflare adapter, where the
# Workers Assets runtime honours `_headers`. HTML is untouched: it is served by
# the worker, not from this directory, and keeps the `s-maxage` OpenNext gives
# it.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
